  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A circuit contains a variable resistor of maximum resistance R and a fixed resistor, also of resistance R, connected in series. The emf of the battery is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0 V\"></span> and its internal resistance is negligible.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What are the initial and final voltmeter readings when the variable resistor is increased from an initial resistance of zero to a final resistance of R?</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
